You definitely need to get healtcheck working before you do anything else, so you are doing the right thing. But, while the healthcheck is quite a simple test, with few moving parts, if you are on a development server, you can simpify it more. Try making a file called test.php with contents like 
```text
<?php
require_once(__DIR__ . '/config.php');
require_once($CFG->
dirroot
 . '/question/type/stack/locallib.php');
require_once($CFG->dirroot . '/question/type/stack/stack/cas/connectorhelper.class.php');

$PAGE->set_url('/test.php');
$PAGE->set_context(context_system::instance());

echo $OUTPUT->header();

$casstrings = [\stack_ast_container::make_from_teacher_source('1+1',
        'test_instantiation_and_return_values()')];
$session = new \stack_cas_session2($casstrings);
$session->instantiate();

$result = $casstrings[0]->get_evaluated()->toString();
print_object($result);

echo $OUTPUT->footer();
```
 Then access that in your browser. And, while doing this turn of the various caching option in the STACK settings, to make sure you are always directly calling goemaxima. Debugging that might be even simpler than debugging the healthcheck page. Really, there are two places the error might be, either goemaxima is not working, or the STACK settings are wrong. If you cant work out which it is, well digging into the above could you should find that in question/type/stack/stack/cas/connector.server.class.php in comes down to a curl call to the goemaxima server. So, can you work out that HTTP request and do the curl call from the command line? That might help find where the problem is.

Hello everyone, (this may be useful for some of you) Use the following code in your STACK question: Question variable : 
```text
rewrite_with_surd(expr) := block([base, exponent, pow_num, non_sqrt, new_expr, simp_save],
    simp_save: simp,
    simp: true,
    if atom(expr) then return(expr),
    if op(expr) = "^" then (
        base: part(expr, 1),
        exponent: part(expr, 2),
        if ratnump(exponent) and denom(exponent) = 2 then (
            pow_num: num(exponent),
            non_sqrt: base^floor(pow_num/2),
            return(non_sqrt*rat(sqrt(base)))
        )
    ),
    new_expr: map(rewrite_with_surd, args(expr)),
    simp: simp_save,
    return(apply(op(expr), new_expr))
);

expr1: 2^((2+3)/2);
expr2: (1 + 2*x^((2+3)/2)) / z;
```
 Question text: 
```text
{@simp: false@}
<p>Original: {@expr1@}, Rewrited: {@rewrite_with_surd(expr1)@}</p>
<p>Original: {@expr2@}, Rewrited: {@rewrite_with_surd(expr2)@}</p>
<p>[ [input:ans1] ] [ [validation:ans1] ]</p>
```
 However, this code has a problem with expressions such as (x+y)^(5/2) . Instead of (x+y)^2*sqrt(y+x), it gives (y^2+2*x*y+x^2)*sqrt(y+x). If anyone knows how to solve this problem (not in Maxima, but in the STACK) by modifying the above code, please let me know. For now, it would be enough if you could help me solve the reversed order of x and y . Thank you.

Hi all, I have found a solution to the first problem: (x+y)^(5/2) = (y+x)^2*sqrt(y+x). 
```text
rewrite_with_surd(expr) := block([base, exponent, pow_num, non_sqrt, new_expr],
    if atom(expr) then return(expr),
    if op(expr) = "^" then (
        base: part(expr, 1),
        exponent: part(expr, 2),
        if ratnump(exponent) and denom(exponent) = 2 then (
            pow_num: num(exponent),
            non_sqrt: ev(base^floor(pow_num/2), simp),
            return(non_sqrt*rat(sqrt(base)))
        )
    ),
    new_expr: map(rewrite_with_surd, args(expr)),
    return(apply(op(expr), new_expr))
);

expr1: 2^((2+3)/2);
expr2: (1 + 2*(x+y)^((2+3)/2)) / z;
```
 But I still don't know how to change the order of variables alphabetically, because this 
```text
{@(ordergreat(x,y), rewrite_with_surd(expr2))@}
```
 does not work.

Finally, I found a solution to all of the above problems. The ordergreat(x, y) command must be placed before simp: false, otherwise it does not work. Here is the latest version of the function in the Question variables section: 
```text
rewrite_with_surd(expr) := block([base, exponent, pow_num, non_sqrt, new_args, second_arg],
    if atom(expr) then return(expr),
    if op(expr) = "^" then (
        base: part(expr, 1),
        exponent: part(expr, 2),
        if ratnump(exponent) and denom(exponent) = 2 then (
            pow_num: num(exponent),
            non_sqrt: ev(base^floor(pow_num/2), simp),
            return(non_sqrt*rat(sqrt(base)))
        )
    ),
    new_args: map(rewrite_with_surd, args(expr)),
    /* If the expression is in the form a*(b*sqrt(c)) return it as (a*b)*sqrt(c) */
    if length(new_args) = 2 and not atom(second(new_args)) then (
        second_arg: args(second(new_args)),
        if not atom(second_arg) and 
           op(expr) = "*" and op(second(new_args)) = "*" then (
            return(ev(first(new_args)*first(second_arg), simp)*second(second_arg))
        )
    ),
    return(apply(op(expr), new_args))
);

ordergreat(x, y, z);
expr1: 3*2^((2+3)/2);
expr2: (1 + 2*(x + y)^((2+3)/2)) / z;
```
 And its use in the Question text section: 
```text
<div style="display: none;">{@simp: false@}</div>
<p>Original: {@expr1@}, Rewritten: {@rewrite_with_surd(expr1)@}</p>
<p>Original: {@expr2@}, Rewritten: {@rewrite_with_surd(expr2)@}</p>
<p>[​[input:ans1]​] [​[validation:ans1]​]</p>
```

